        "Automation makes this reliable rather than a matter of someone remembering to check back. With {{post:auto-verify-with-sentinel-app}}, the KODA Sentinel Android app reads the operator's payment SMS or notification the instant it arrives and forwards it automatically to the engine. So the merchant does not have to babysit a pending order or re-run anything by hand — the delayed confirmation flows in on its own and closes the loop the moment the network catches up. A payment that was 'pending' at the counter becomes 'verified-late' without anyone lifting a finger.",
        "It is essential that patience never becomes a loophole, and it does not. A late confirmation is not waved through just because it arrived after a delay. Every confirmation, on time or late, must first clear the {{post:balance-chain-fake-sms}} anti-forgery defence and pass the same fraud scoring and velocity rules as an instant one. Forgers sometimes bet that a system relaxes its guard for stragglers; KODA does the opposite, applying the full battery of checks regardless of timing. Late is a timing state, not a trust discount.",
